NOTICE — 最後的皇朝：康雍乾盛世

This is an original classroom exploration game. The palace setting is a
紫禁城風格 scene inspired by an imperial court. It is not an official
product of the Forbidden City / Palace Museum, not a scan or replica of
the real palace, and not a reproduction of any publisher’s textbook.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3D architecture and garden models
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pack:    Imperial China Palace and Garden
Source:  https://3dassets.dev/packs/imperial-china-palace-and-garden
Licence: CC0 1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/)

Every model used in the game is stored in public/assets/models/ and loaded
from this repository at runtime (not from a CDN). A file-by-file list with
asset ids, source pages and original CDN URLs is in
public/assets/models/SOURCES.txt.

Starter courtyard (Kangxi / Yongzheng palace ground):
  courtyard.glb  (asset 36222)
  https://3dassets.dev/assets/imperial-china-palace-and-garden-walled--b51639b8-starter-scene

Other placed pieces include the ceremonial hall, gate tower, imperial
throne (36199), footstool, guardian lions, banners, chests, writing desk,
folding screen, cauldron, lanterns, rocks, trees, pavilions, and walls,
plus later additions: stone balustrade runs (36174), lotus pond edges
(36181, 36183), floating water lanterns (36189), peony planters (36198),
stepping-stone paths (36197), covered walkway bays/corners (36167, 36168),
latticed screen doors (36182), dragon roof finials (36179), and hall
furnishings (tea table 36201, tea set 36202, guqin 36203, inkstone 36205,
hanging scroll pair 36208, bronze bell 36215). See SOURCES.txt for the
complete list. Training dummy (36212) and pond water module (36184) are
not used.


